{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "קשורה", :translit "k'shurah", :gloss "bound / tied"} {:he "ב' במסורה", :translit "bet ba-masorah", :gloss "twice in the Masorah"} {:he "הכא", :translit "haka", :gloss "here"} {:he "אולת קשורה בלב נער", :translit "ivlet k'shurah b'lev na'ar", :gloss "folly bound in the heart of a youth"} {:he "נער", :translit "na'ar", :gloss "youth / lad"} {:he "אולת", :translit "ivlet", :gloss "folly"} {:he "אולתו", :translit "ivlito", :gloss "his folly"} {:he "קשורה בו", :translit "k'shurah bo", :gloss "bound in him"} {:he "נפשו", :translit "nafsho", :gloss "his soul"} {:he "קשורה בנפשו של אביו", :translit "k'shurah b'nafsho shel aviv", :gloss "bound to the soul of his father"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["קשורה" "אולת קשורה בלב נער"]}], :frame {:text "The term נער connotes immaturity susceptible to folly. Proverbs 22:15 states אולת קשורה בלב נער, 'folly is bound in the heart of a youth.' The midrashic reading draws on this verse to characterize Binyamin's possible taking of the goblet as a product of youthful אולת rather than malice. The alternative reading — that precisely because his אולת is bound in him his soul must be bound to his father's soul — reflects the educational principle of Proverbs 22:6, חנוך לנער על פי דרכו, 'train the youth according to his way,' read here as requiring paternal attachment to guide a child whose inherent folly demands correction.", :sources ["Proverbs 22:15" "Proverbs 22:6"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["קשורה" "אולת קשורה בלב נער"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "קשורה", :refs ["Genesis 44:30" "Proverbs 22:15"], :n 2, :lens :exact} {:phrase "אולת קשורה בלב נער", :refs ["Proverbs 22:15"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:11:37.261774213Z", :model "glm-5.2"}